      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing LLM Provider**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google's Gemini for the hosted LLM. It offers a well-known, accessible platform to build upon. This provides a clear starting point for development.\n\n\n**Defining the Code Structure**\n\nI'm now focusing on outlining the structure for `summarize_text.py`. The plan is to start with the file creation and then embed the Google Generative AI integration, specifically Gemini. I'll need to define the function to manage text summarization. Environment variables will ensure secure API key access, and I'll keep the design straightforward.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820369168,
          "start": 1789820367193
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b99b7159001r1vK71N1Edhi3M",
      "message_id": "msg_0b99b6ae8001RopR3F8BBKnFDE",
      "session_id": "ses_f4664959cffehjXs7wtPojxr9y",
      "time_created": 1789820367193,
      "time_updated": 1789820369169
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "vBYPTTqVOUUsyY4i",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import os\nimport google.generativeai as genai\n\ndef summarize_text(text: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calls a hosted LLM (Google Gemini Pro) to summarize long text.\n    \"\"\"\n    genai.configure(api_key=os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_API_KEY\"))\n\n    model = genai.GenerativeModel(\"gemini-pro\")\n\n    prompt = f\"Please summarize the following text:\n\n{text}\"\n\n    response = model.generate_content(prompt)\n    return response.text\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example usage (replace with your actual long text)\n    long_text = \"\"\"\n    Your very long text goes here. This could be an article, a document,\n    or any other text that you want to summarize using the LLM.\n    Make sure the text is sufficiently long to benefit from summarization.\n    For instance, you might include several paragraphs about a topic,\n    discussing various aspects and details that you want condensed into a\n    shorter, more digestible form. The purpose of this script is to\n    demonstrate how to interact with a hosted LLM for text summarization\n    tasks, making it easy to integrate into other applications or workflows.\n    \"\"\"\n    summary = summarize_text(long_text)\n    print(\"Summary:\")\n    print(summary)\n",
            "filePath": "summarize_text.py"
          },
